		(object Attribute
		    tool       	"Java"
		    name       	"GenerateDefaultConstructor"
		    value      	FALSE))
	    quid       	"36BB22B9029F"
	    documentation 	
|Defines the Interface for a public 'copy' Method.
| * This Method performs a DeepCopy and complements the 'copyAt' Method.
| * It replaces the 'clone' Method (for Object it is only protected).
| * 
| * Since this is the basic Group for all Objects here, 
| * it is never used for Delegation, so the Delegation Stuff is not necessary.
| * 
| * Design Decisions:
| * (De-) Serialization can happen by using the toText and fromText Methods 
| * in a generic way!
| * I have chosen to have the Output sent out to Strings, instead of Streams, 
| * because Strings can simple be written into Output Streams. 
| * That cannot be done on Reading a String, because the Length may vary!
| * 
| * Checking for EOF AND EOL, because it can be switched in the StreamTokenizer,
| * whether EOL is significant or not!
| * 
| * self is not used for Delegation since absCopyAble is mostly the Base Class.
| * 
| * TODO: copyAt(InputStream) and fromStreamAt() do the same, can be delegated! 
	    
	    realized_interfaces 	(list realize_rel_list
		(object Realize_Relationship
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD1B64006A"
		    supplier   	"Logical View::BaseCopy::copyAble"
		    quidu      	"36BB22B9021D"))
	    operations 	(list Operations
		(object Operation "copy"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD1B6400BC"
		    documentation 	
|Creates a new object of the same class as this object. It then 
|	 * initializes each of the new object's fields by assigning it the 
|	 * same value as the corresponding field in this object. No 
|	 * constructor is called. 
|	 * <p>
|	 * The <code>copy</code> method of class <code>Object</code> will 
|	 * only copy an object whose class indicates that it is willing for 
|	 * its instances to be cloned. A class indicates that its instances 
|	 * can be cloned by declaring that it implements the 
|	 * <code>Cloneable</code> interface. 
|	 * 
|	 * @return     a copy of this instance.
|	 * @exception  CloneNotSupportedException  if the object's class does not
|	 * support the <code>Cloneable</code> interface. Subclasses
|	 * that override the <code>copy</code> method can also
|	 * throw this exception to indicate that an instance cannot
|	 * be cloned.
|	 * @exception  OutOfMemoryError            if there is not enough memory.
|	 * @see        java.lang.Cloneable
|	 * @since      JDK1.0	 
		    
		    result     	"copyAble"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "shallowCopy"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD1B6400C3"
		    documentation 	
|Creates a new shallow Copy of this Instance.
|	 * I.e. both Instances will share their inner Components.
|	 * shallowCopy also clones the Types, but does not initialize them!
|	 * rarely used.
|	 * This is the Default Implementation and should always work, 
|	 * although a direct Implementation could be faster.	 
		    
		    result     	"copyAble"
		    concurrency 	"Sequential"
		    opExportControl 	"Public"
		    uid        	0)
		(object Operation "copy"
		    attributes 	(list Attribute_Set)
		    quid       	"37BD1B6400C4"
		    documentation 	
|Complement to copy() and shallopCopy().
|	 * Does a 'deepCopy', to a certain Level
